From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a GPU with no 3D draws the desktop on the CPU

On 2D virtio-gpu, Hyper-V, simpledrm and vkms the GPU process has no GL,
so viz composites in software. ozone/drm had no software output:
`GbmSurfaceFactory::CreateCanvasForWidget` returned null after logging
`Software rendering mode is not supported with GBM platform`, and viz
crashed on the CHECK after it.

- `DrmCanvas` (`domicile/drm_canvas.{h,cc}`) is the `SurfaceOzoneCanvas`.
  Viz paints into a frame in memory; each present copies what changed into
  one of two XRGB8888 dumb buffers and flips the window's CRTC to it. The
  dumb buffers are only written, since on hardware they are
  write-combined.
- A buffer misses the frames presented while the other was in use, so
  each keeps the region it is stale by and a present copies that too.
- A swap is acknowledged when its flip lands (`MaxFramesPending` 1), so
  viz never paints into the buffer on screen.
- `SWAP_NAK_RECREATE_BUFFERS` (the window moved to another card)
  reallocates both buffers on the next present.
- `DrmThread::DomicileCreateScanoutBuffer` allocates on the device that
  drives the widget, through `DrmThreadProxy` as `CreateBuffer` does.
- A card with no 3D may have no GBM: mesa has no driver for simpledrm,
  and on 2D virtio-gpu the GPU process failed `gbm_create_device`, so it
  had no DRM device and crashed on a DCHECK. `GbmDeviceGenerator` now keeps
  such a device, logged. `ScreenManager` modesets it with a dumb buffer;
  GBM buffers on it fail, logged.
- `DrmCanvasTest` runs in ozone_unittests on a `FakeDrmDevice`, and
  `DrmNoGbmModesetTest` on one with no GBM
  (`screen_manager_unittest.cc` builds only on ChromeOS).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
